//- AI-GENERATED — not an architecture reference
//- The guest's half of an assisted registration (EM-013): the account already exists
//- and the password is already set — this mail only asks the guest to prove the
//- address is theirs. Deliberately NOT the accountActivation template: that one talks
//- about finishing the registration by choosing a password, which here is already done.
extend ../layout.pug

block content
  h2= t('emails.assistedRegistrationConfirm.title')
  .text-block
    include ../includes/salutation.pug
    p
      = t('emails.assistedRegistrationConfirm.accountCreated')
      br
      = t('emails.assistedRegistrationConfirm.pleaseConfirm')
  .content
    h2= t('emails.assistedRegistrationConfirm.confirmHeading')
    div(class="p_content")= t('emails.assistedRegistrationConfirm.clickToConfirm')
    a.button-3(href=confirmLink) #{t('emails.assistedRegistrationConfirm.confirmButton')}
    div(class="p_content")= t('emails.general.orCopyLink')

    a.clink(href=confirmLink) #{confirmLink}

    //- Deliberately NO requestNewLink include: its button leads to the forgot-password
    //- page, which flips the opt-in row to RESET and would disarm this very confirm
    //- link. Resending lives in the wallet's reminder modal instead. The validity
    //- lines stay — they answer "how long is this link good for".
    if timeDurationObject.minutes == 0
      div(class="p_content")= t('emails.general.linkValidity', { hours: timeDurationObject.hours })
    else
      div(class="p_content")= t('emails.general.linkValidityWithMinutes', { hours: timeDurationObject.hours, minutes: timeDurationObject.minutes })

    div(class="p_content")= t('emails.assistedRegistrationConfirm.notYou')
